Idira Secrets Manager Credential Providers V15.2 Release
 
Hi Benjamin
We are pleased to announce the release of Idira® Secrets Manager Credential Providers version 15.2, a Short-Term Support (STS) release introducing new and enhanced features.
This version updates its Object Module library to a validated FIPS 140-3 certified version to meet stringent government compliance standards. Additionally, it introduces robust IPv6 address support for Credential Providers communicating with Idira Privileged Access Manager Self-Hosted vaults across Windows, RHEL, Oracle, CentOS, and Ubuntu platforms.
 
Key New Features and Capabilities Improvements:
Federal Information Processing Standards (FIPS) compliance
Idira has updated the current Object Module library to a validated FIPS certified version (140-3) in order to comply with government requirements and regulations. For more information, see FIPS compliance.

IPv6 support for Credential Providers on Idira Privileged Access Manager Self-Hosted
We are happy to introduce Credential Providers support for IPv6 addresses when communicating with an Idira Privileged Access Manager Self-Hosted Vault:
This capability includes:
•	Support for IPv6/IPv4 Vaults
•	Support for Credential Providers running on IPV6 and IPv6/IPv4 machines
This capability is available for the Central Credential Provider and Credential Provider on Windows, RHEL, Oracle, CentOS, and Ubuntu.
This capability is in addition to the IPv6 application authentication that was introduced in version 14.0.
